<!-- IronStone People (design-people §1): the root of the app for HR officers, managers, recruiters, payroll and development
    staff, case handlers and the People administrator. The root user group BOSS_PEOPLE and the administrator group
    BOSS_PEOPLE_ADMIN open it (data/BossSetupData.xml), as ADMIN does; BOSS_PEOPLE_SELF has no root grant (an employee's
    self-service is Commons', impl-people P8). The root grant opens navigation only: ironstone.people.ContextServices
    .get#SharedContext checks the user and resolves their capabilities, employers, units, own employments and links for every
    subscreen, and each Mantle service (mantle.humanres.PeopleServices) checks the scope again. The menu of design §1.2 grows by
    phase: P1 builds Home (every People user's) and Settings (the People administrator's, BOSS_PPL_SETTINGS); P2 Employees (the
    directory and Employee360, every People user's, each seeing what Mantle's scope admits); P3 Organization and Org chart under
    Employees (OrgStructure and OrgChart, every People user's, changed by HR editors); P4 Positions & recruiting (Staffing:
    Positions, Job classes and Pay grades, every People user's, a grade's amounts payroll's alone); P5 Approvals (the Commons
    Notifications list of People's approval topics, every People user's own) and the Settings tabs Approval rules and Lookups
    (the People administrator's); each later phase adds its entries,
    and the design's later entries stay absent. P2 adds the palette's directory and the Person record-lookup; P6 the quick create
    "Hire employee" (HR's: the wizard's grant decides who sees it) and the employment change topic; P8 My team (the managers',
    BOSS_PPL_TEAM) and the key g m, SelfService out of the menu (the user's own, also Commons'), Today's decisions waiting on the
    user and the PeopleTaskAssigned topic; P9 Working schedules and Holidays under Time & leave (HR's and the managers',
    BOSS_PPL_SCHEDULES; Holidays HR's alone, BOSS_PPL_HOLIDAYS) and the key g w; P10 Time & leave's time screens (Projects' mounted
    under People/Time: Timesheets, My time, Time entries, every People user's and a self-service employee's by the area's own grant,
    BOSS_PPL_TIME), Payroll (Projects' Rates
    under People/Payroll, the payroll groups', BOSS_PPL_PAYROLL), the keys g t and g r, the timesheet topics and Today's weeks to
    submit; P11 Leave balances (HR's and the managers') and HR's Leave policies and Allocations under Time & leave
    (BOSS_PPL_LEAVE_BALANCES, BOSS_PPL_LEAVE) and the key g b; P12 Leave requests and the Team calendar under Time & leave (every
    People user's and a self-service employee's, by the area's grant), the quick create Request leave, the leave topics, the palette's
    own leave requests, the LeaveRequest record-lookup (the people.records provider), Today's leave starting for my team, the key g l
    and the prompt "Explain my balance"; P13 Attendance under Time & leave (every People user's and a self-service employee's, by the
    area's grant) with HR's Time import (BOSS_PPL_TIME_IMPORT) and the Clock in screen (the quick create, declared on Commons' root),
    the attendance topic and the key g d; P14 the Shift roster under Time & leave (HR's and the managers', BOSS_PPL_SCHEDULES), the
    worker's shift topic and the key g h; P15 Expenses (Expense claims, with ExpenseClaimDetail and its print, and Advances; every
    People user's and a self-service employee's, by the area's grant BOSS_PPL_EXPENSES), Payroll's InvoiceDetail (an expense claim's
    invoice for payroll), the expense and advance topics, the key g x and the quick create New claim (declared on Commons' root).
    The Chatter and RecordFiles panels under this root open only People's own record hosts (the
    employment, P2; each later host with its phase): any other record's notes and files are kept in its own app, so the root's
    grant opens no other record's panel. P16: Openings, Applicants and Interviews under Positions &amp; recruiting (every People
    user's: a recruiter reads the openings and applications, an interviewer the applications of their panels), Forms under Settings
    (the People administrator's), the application's files (its RecordFiles host), the palette's openings and applications and the
    EmploymentApplication record-lookup (the people.records provider), the keys g n and g v, and the prompt "Draft a job
    description" (the people-job-description skill) on a job class and on Openings. P18 Skills and training (Development: the
    skills matrix with its terminal twin, and Qualifications, every People user's and a self-service employee's by the area's
    grant, BOSS_PPL_DEVELOPMENT; the matrix denied to self-service, BOSS_PPL_SKILLS), the qualification content host (a
    qualification's files, its RecordFiles and Chatter host), the QualificationExpiring topic and the keys g k and g q. P19 Training
    under Skills and training (sessions, a session's detail and a completed place's certificate, every People user's and a
    self-service employee's by the area's grant), the PeopleTrainingApproval topic and Today's training due; its review: the
    PeopleTrainingDecision topic, the key g i and the Assessment forms under Skills and training (BOSS_PPL_ASSESSMENT_FORMS). P21
    Grievances under Employees (every People user's and a self-service employee's by its own grant, BOSS_PPL_CASES_SELF), a case's
    RequestDetail (Shared/RequestDetail with People's branch, its people's alone), the case as a record panel host (its notes and
    files) and the PeopleCaseUpdate topic; no palette source, search, record-lookup or Assist tool answers a case. P20 Reviews & goals
    (Performance: Reviews, Goals, every People user's and a self-service employee's by the area's grant, BOSS_PPL_PERFORMANCE; Review
    cycles and Review forms the review administrator's, BOSS_PPL_REVIEW_ADMIN), a review as a record panel host (its files and notes,
    the reviewer's, development's and, once released, the person's; never the reviewer's private notes, which are not Chatter), the
    PeopleReviewStep and PeopleReviewUpdate topics and the key g f. -->
<screen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/xml-screen-3.xsd"
        default-menu-title="People" menu-image="sym_o_groups" menu-image-type="icon">

    <always-actions>
        <set field="appRoot" value="People"/>

        <service-call name="mantle.party.PartyServices.setup#UserOrganizationInfo" out-map="context"/>
        <service-call name="ironstone.people.ContextServices.get#SharedContext" in-map="{appRoot:appRoot}" out-map="people"/>
        <set field="sharedLinks" from="people.sharedLinks"/>
        <!-- P2: the record panels serve People's HR hosts only (design §13 Chatter and RecordFiles; F66); a panel request with no
            record (a person search, an avatar) names none -->
        <script><![CDATA[
            const pathNames = Array.from(sri.getScreenUrlInfo().fullPathNameList || []).map(String)
            const panelName = pathNames[pathNames.indexOf('People') + 1]
            const wanted = ec.context.recordEntity
            if ((panelName === 'Chatter' || panelName === 'RecordFiles') && wanted) {
                let entityName = String(wanted)
                try { entityName = ec.entity.makeValue(entityName).getEntityName() } catch (error) { entityName = '' }
                // P16: an application's files; P18: a qualification's files (its content host, the person's and HR's); P21: a
                // confidential case's notes and files (its people's, Mantle's record rule), never another request's; P20: a review's
                // files and notes (its content host, Mantle's check#ReviewAccess)
                const confidentialCase = entityName === 'mantle.request.Request' && !!ec.context.recordId && ec.resource
                        .script('component://mr-mantle/service/mantle/request/PeopleCases.js').isCase(String(ec.context.recordId))
                if (!confidentialCase && !['mantle.humanres.employment.Employment', 'mantle.humanres.employment.EmploymentApplication',
                        'mantle.humanres.ability.PartyQualification', 'mantle.humanres.ability.PerformanceReview'].includes(entityName))
                    throw new Error('RECORD_PANEL_UNAVAILABLE: Notes and files of this record are kept in the app that owns it')
            }
        ]]></script>
    </always-actions>

    <subscreens default-item="Home" always-use-full-path="true">
        <!-- the record panels the chatter and record-files elements load under this app root, hidden from the menu
            (the theme values STRT_CHATTER_SCREEN and STRT_RECORD_FILES_SCREEN; impl-drawers-commons.md R5) -->
        <subscreens-item name="Chatter" location="component://mr-boss/screen/Shared/Chatter.xml" menu-include="false"/>
        <subscreens-item name="RecordFiles" location="component://mr-boss/screen/Shared/RecordFiles.xml" menu-include="false"/>
        <!-- P8: the user's own self-service (design §3 SelfService), the same definition as Commons/People/SelfService, out of the
            menu and linked from Home; a self-service employee without People opens it by its own grant (BOSS_PPL_SELF) -->
        <subscreens-item name="SelfService" location="component://mr-boss/screen/Shared/PeopleSelfService.xml" menu-include="false"/>
        <!-- P16 review (the user's call of Nov 12, 2026): an interview panel member's own interview and scorecard, beside SelfService
            and opened from its My interviews, the same definition as Commons/People/MyInterview -->
        <subscreens-item name="MyInterview" location="component://mr-boss/screen/Shared/PeopleMyInterview.xml" menu-include="false"/>
    </subscreens>

    <!-- P1: the people keymap (P3: g o and g c; P4: g s; P5: g a; P8: g m; P9: g w; P10: g t and g r; P11: g b; P14: g h; P16: g n and g v; P18: g k and g q). P2: the palette's directory (Employees, as Commons' People group is its contacts) and the Person
        record-lookup over the directory projection (design §1.4). Quick create and Today (design §1.4) come with their records. -->
    <shell-providers>
        <palette-source group="Employees" label="Employee directory" icon="sym_o_badge"
                service="ironstone.people.ContextServices.search#Records" sequence="25"/>
        <record-lookup name="people.records" service="ironstone.people.ContextServices.lookup#Records" sequence="30"/>
        <keymap scope="people">
            <key keys="g p" label="People home" screen="People/Home"/>
            <key keys="g e" label="Employees" screen="People/Employees"/>
            <key keys="g o" label="Organization" screen="People/Employees/OrgStructure"/>
            <key keys="g c" label="Org chart" screen="People/Employees/OrgChart"/>
            <key keys="g s" label="Positions" screen="People/Staffing/Positions"/>
            <key keys="g a" label="Approvals" screen="People/Approvals"/>
            <key keys="g m" label="My team" screen="People/MyTeam"/>
            <!-- P9: the working schedules; P10: the timesheets and payroll's rates; P11: the leave balances -->
            <key keys="g w" label="Working schedules" screen="People/Time/WorkingSchedules"/>
            <key keys="g t" label="Timesheets" screen="People/Time/Timesheets"/>
            <key keys="g r" label="Rates" screen="People/Payroll/Rates"/>
            <key keys="g b" label="Leave balances" screen="People/Time/LeaveBalances"/>
            <!-- P12: the leave requests -->
            <key keys="g l" label="Leave requests" screen="People/Time/LeaveRequests"/>
            <!-- P13: attendance -->
            <key keys="g d" label="Attendance" screen="People/Time/Attendance"/>
            <!-- P14: the shift roster -->
            <key keys="g h" label="Shift roster" screen="People/Time/ShiftRoster"/>
            <!-- P15: expense claims -->
            <key keys="g x" label="Expense claims" screen="People/Expenses/ExpenseClaims"/>
            <!-- P16: the openings and the interviews -->
            <key keys="g n" label="Openings" screen="People/Staffing/Openings"/>
            <key keys="g v" label="Interviews" screen="People/Staffing/InterviewsCalendar"/>
            <!-- P18: the skills matrix and the qualifications -->
            <key keys="g k" label="Skills matrix" screen="People/Development/SkillsMatrix"/>
            <key keys="g q" label="Qualifications" screen="People/Development/Qualifications"/>
            <!-- P19 review: the training sessions -->
            <key keys="g i" label="Training" screen="People/Development/Training"/>
            <!-- P20: the reviews -->
            <key keys="g f" label="Reviews" screen="People/Performance/Reviews"/>
        </keymap>
        <!-- P5: a position's activation to approve (Mantle's PeoplePositionApproval), for the Notifications panel's filter by app -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeoplePositionApproval"/>
        <!-- P6: a transfer or separation to approve (PeopleEmploymentChangeApproval), and the quick create Hire employee for HR
            (design §1.4), opening the hire wizard, which the HR officers' grant opens (BOSS_PPL_EMPLOYMENT) -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleEmploymentChangeApproval"/>
        <quick-create kind="peopleHireEmployee" label="Hire employee" icon="sym_o_person_add" screen="People/Employees/HireEmployee"
                sequence="95"/>
        <!-- P8: Today's decisions waiting on the user (design §1.4 Today), also declared on Commons' root for a self-service
            employee, who opens no People root (F64): one service, taken once; and a People task assigned (PeopleTaskAssigned) -->
        <today-source service="ironstone.people.ContextServices.get#TodayItems" label="People"/>
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleTaskAssigned"/>
        <!-- P10: the timesheet topics of Projects' time screens, mounted under People/Time (Today's weeks to submit are the source above) -->
        <notification-topic topic="TimesheetApproval"/>
        <notification-topic topic="TimesheetReturned"/>
        <notification-topic topic="TimesheetApproved"/>
        <notification-topic topic="TimesheetMissing"/>
        <!-- P12 (design §1.4): leave to approve (PeopleLeaveApproval), the person's decision notice (PeopleLeaveDecision), the quick
            create Request leave (every People user's: the area's grant opens it; a self-service employee reaches it from their
            self-service page), and "Explain my balance" on a request and on the balances (the people-leave-balance skill, answered
            from the user's own people_my_leave_balances tool: an approver or HR reads another person's balance on the page) -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleLeaveApproval"/>
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleLeaveDecision"/>
        <quick-create kind="peopleRequestLeave" label="Request leave" icon="sym_o_event_busy" screen="People/Time/LeaveRequests"
                sequence="96"><parameter name="request" value="Y"/></quick-create>
        <assist-prompt label="Explain my balance" text="Explain my leave balance: what I was granted, accrued, took and have reserved, and what is left"
                screen="People/Time/LeaveRequestDetail" sequence="40"/>
        <assist-prompt label="Explain my balance" text="Explain my leave balance: what I was granted, accrued, took and have reserved, and what is left"
                screen="People/Time/LeaveBalances" sequence="41"/>
        <!-- P13: an attendance correction to approve (PeopleAttendanceApproval); the quick create Clock in is declared on Commons' root,
            which a self-service employee opens too -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleAttendanceApproval"/>
        <!-- P14: a worker's shifts published, changed or removed (PeopleShiftChange) -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleShiftChange"/>
        <!-- P15: an expense claim and an employee advance to approve (PeopleExpenseApproval, PeopleAdvanceApproval); the quick create
            New claim is declared on Commons' root, which a self-service employee opens too -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleExpenseApproval"/>
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleAdvanceApproval"/>
        <!-- P16 (design §5 JobClassDetail, Openings; PE-14): "Draft a job description" (the people-job-description skill) on a job
            class and on the openings, the user's own draft to read and paste: nothing is saved by it -->
        <assist-prompt label="Draft a job description" text="Draft a job description for this role from its job class: the purpose, the main responsibilities, the skills it requires and what it offers, in plain words"
                screen="People/Staffing/JobClassDetail" sequence="42"/>
        <assist-prompt label="Draft a job description" text="Draft the description of a job opening: the role, what it asks and what it offers, in plain words, without pay figures or anything about age, gender or family"
                screen="People/Staffing/Openings" sequence="43"/>
        <!-- P18: the person's own qualification expiring (QualificationExpiring, Mantle's daily reminder; Today's item is the source above) -->
        <notification-topic topic="QualificationExpiring"/>
        <!-- P17: an offer of employment to approve (PeopleOfferApproval), opening OfferDetail -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleOfferApproval"/>
        <!-- P19: a place in a training session to approve (PeopleTrainingApproval; DevelopmentServices approve#Enrollment and
            refuse#Enrollment), opening the session; Today's training due is the source above -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleTrainingApproval"/>
        <!-- P19 review: the person's decision notice (PeopleTrainingDecision), opening their place -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleTrainingDecision"/>
        <!-- P21: a confidential case filed with, assigned to or changed for one of its people (PeopleCaseUpdate: no push, a title that
            names nothing) -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleCaseUpdate"/>
        <!-- P20: a review's finalizing to approve (PeopleReviewStep; ReviewServices approve#ReviewStep and refuse#ReviewStep), and a review
            step given, returned or a review released (PeopleReviewUpdate: a sentence, never a rating, an answer or a note) -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleReviewStep"/>
        <notification-topic topic="PeopleReviewUpdate"/>
        <!-- P24: a pay adjustment to approve (PeoplePayAdjustmentApproval; PayrollInputServices approve#Adjustment and
            refuse#Adjustment), a title naming no person and no amount -->
        <notification-topic topic="PeoplePayAdjustmentApproval"/>
    </shell-providers>

    <widgets><subscreens-panel id="people-panel" type="popup"/></widgets>
</screen>
